  "narrative_llm": "<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Short impact summary</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Stilte in de klas shows clear signs of use beyond citation tracking: it has been downloaded 2,627 times and is being discussed in at least one recorded teaching-related video, suggesting steady readership and pedagogical interest. The book is also available as open access through a hybrid model, which likely supports its reach in education-focused and humanities-oriented audiences.</p>\n<h3 class=\"story-subheading\">Full narrative</h3>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Pieter Verstraete\u2019s Stilte in de klas is a historically grounded study of the educational meaning of silence, drawing on previously untapped archival material to trace how classroom quietness has been discussed and valued over time. The record shows a strong fit with Quality Education and a clear policy- and practice-facing relevance: a topic like classroom silence speaks directly to pedagogy, teacher formation, and how learning environments are organized.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">In terms of uptake, the most visible signal is usage rather than citation. The book has been downloaded 2,627 times, indicating sustained interest from readers. It is also referenced in a 2025 YouTube video associated with a PPW Continue talk, which suggests that the book has entered teaching and professional discussion contexts. Together, these signals point to a work that is being read and talked about in educational settings, even though its formal citation record is still early.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Open access availability likely supports that reach, since the book is recorded as openly accessible in a hybrid publication model. The publication is linked to KU Leuven through funding, and its subject profile aligns most strongly with theology, art, and philosophy, underscoring the book\u2019s interdisciplinary framing of silence as both a pedagogical and cultural concept.</p>\n<p class=\"story-text\">Overall, the evidence portrays a book with meaningful educational relevance and visible reader interest, especially through downloads and teaching-related discussion. The citation count remains at zero in the current record, so scholarly citation-based influence has not yet emerged here; for now, the impact story is mainly one of access, use, and conceptual relevance in education.</p>",
